-- Classic and TBC instance spawn masks (5.4.8 mask bits: 2 = 5-player normal, 4 = 5-player heroic,
-- 8 = 10-player, 16 = 25-player, 512 = 40-player).
-- Molten Core, Blackwing Lair and Temple of Ahn'Qiraj only have the 40-player difficulty (MapDifficulty.dbc), but every
-- spawn there had spawnMask 0, which spawns in no difficulty. They get 512 (the core change in this PR makes these
-- raids run as 40-player whatever raid difficulty the group has set).
-- In the TBC heroic dungeons a few heroic-only spawns were normal only, and the difficulty-portal doodads were too.
-- Each spawn gets the mask of the matching spawn (same entry within 5 yards) in:
--   1. Legends of Azeroth Pandaria 5.4.8 (GPL v2), world DB of 2024-07-22
--   2. TrinityCore TDB 3.3.5 (GPL v2); a spawn in a single-difficulty map gets that map's mask, a 5-player one 1/2 -> 2/4
-- else the mask LoA gives every spawn of that entry on the map, else (entry LoA never spawns there) the map's full mask.
-- Generated by skyfire_port_plan/tools/raidmasks.py (--from 0 for 409/469/531, --from 2 for the TBC dungeons).
-- No database names; safe to run twice.

